course: dictionary
lesson: 7439
title: Polonium: a rare, dangerous element
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Polonium is a chemical element. An element is a pure substance that cannot be broken into simpler substances by ordinary means. Each element has its own number and symbol: polonium is number 84, and its symbol is Po.
explain: Polonium is rare and extremely radioactive, which means it gives out invisible rays of energy. It is also poisonous, so only experts with special equipment ever handle it.
explain: Marie Curie discovered polonium, with Pierre Curie. «Marie Curie discovered two new elements, polonium and radium, separating tiny amounts of them from tonnes of ore.» She named it after Poland, her home country.
fact: An element is a substance made of only one kind of atom, and the periodic table lists them all.
fact: Polonium is element number 84, and its symbol is Po.
fact: Polonium is uncountable: we say some polonium, not a polonium.
fact: «Radioactive» means giving out invisible rays of energy, and «poisonous» means harmful to living things if swallowed or touched.
fact: Marie Curie named polonium after Poland, her home country.
exercise: What is the symbol for polonium? | *Po | Pl | Pm | Pu
exercise: «Marie Curie discovered two new elements, polonium and radium.» What is an element? | A kind of rock found under the sea | A loud noise made by machines | *A pure substance made of one kind of atom | A mixture of many metals
exercise: Why is polonium handled only by experts? | *It is poisonous and extremely radioactive | It is too pretty to touch | It is common in every kitchen | It is a liquid that spills easily
test: Which scientist named polonium after her home country? | *Marie Curie | Pierre Curie | Dmitri Mendeleev | Henri Becquerel
test: Which word means harmful to living things if swallowed or touched? | Radium | Rare | Radioactive | *Poisonous
exam: Which element has the symbol Po and the number 84? | Plutonium | *Polonium | Radon | Radium
